      "message": "fix(post): sinker ISO post writes the document's unit, not the machine file's\n\nsinker-iso.cps decided inch/mm from `machine.units`; since #902 the\nprogram's unit is the document's (`postOptions.Units`). It now reads\npostOptions.Units, as wire-iso.cps does, and declares\n`programUnits = \"mm inch\"` (its lengths and feeds already convert, and\nthe unit word is the machine's edm.codes.metric / edm.codes.inch, an\ninch document on a machine stating no inch code refused by name).\n\nPinned by script_sinker_iso's\nthe_sinker_program_posts_in_the_documents_unit_not_the_machine_files\n(an inch machine file under an mm document posts the mm golden byte for\nbyte; an inch document writes G20 and every length / 25.4). The\nmissing-inch-code refusal now asks an inch document, not an inch\nmachine file. program_units' machine-file law is green again.\n\nFixes #1382\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
